      "body": "PR Title:[Fix] moe: Preserve expert recording with TRT-LLM routing\n## Motivation\n\nFixes #47932.\n\nWhen FlashInfer TRT-LLM is used with expert distribution recording enabled, SGLang can still select `BYPASSED` routing. Since expert selection happens inside the TRT-LLM kernel, the normal `select_experts` path is skipped, along with the expert distribution recorder hook.\n\nAs a result, the server can process requests normally while reporting zero expert counts. This makes the recorded statistics unreliable when monitoring expert usage.\n\n## Modifications\n\nThis PR makes a small change to `TopK.bind_runner_backend`:\n\n- Use `TopKOutputFormat.STANDARD` for FlashInfer TRT-LLM when expert distribution recording is enabled, allowing the recorder to observe expert selection.\n- Keep the existing `BYPASSED` routing when recording is disabled.\n- Leave the FlashInfer MXFP4 routing behavior unchanged.\n- Add a CPU regression test covering all four recording modes (`stat`, `stat_approx`, `per_pass`, and `per_token`), as well as the default behavior with recording disabled.\n\nThe aim is to make expert distribution recording work correctly without changing the normal inference path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAdded a registered CPU regression test to check routing format selection across all four recording modes and when recording is disabled.\n\nThe test has not yet been executed in a full SGLang development environment. End-to-end inference accuracy validation is also pending.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance benchmarks have been run yet.\n\nNormal inference with recording disabled retains the existing routing path, so no performance change is intended for that configuration.\n\nWhen recording is enabled, standard routing may introduce additional overhead compared to the in-kernel bypass. This has not yet been measured.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Patch applied successfully.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Python syntax checked in isolation.\n- Changes committed and pushed successfully.\n- Registered CPU test execution and end-to-end validation are pending.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Run the full pre-commit formatting checks.\n- [x] Add a registered CPU regression test.\n- [ ] Update documentation (no documentation changes currently needed).\n- [ ] Complete applicable accuracy and performance validation.\n- [ ] Run the project's full code-style checks.\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\nThis is a narrowly scoped bug fix addressing the missing expert distribution statistics reported in #47932.\n\nI would appreciate feedback on the approach, especially whether switching to standard routing when recording is enabled is the preferred way to handle this.\n\nCI and runtime validation are still pending.\n\nThanks for reviewing!\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41622201955](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41622201955)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41622201884](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41622201884)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41622201951](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41622201951)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
